From df9297f42bb08493ddd9c19686cca65a4947db01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:34:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerAudio: sleep when the sink has nothing to wait on

The wait on the message queue is as long as the audio sink has data
cached, so a starved stream waits for nothing at all, and the decoder has
nothing to hand over either. The branch that covers this already sleeps,
but the early return taken while paused or waiting to sync jumps over it,
and the thread then runs flat out: one core at 100% for as long as the
source cannot keep up.

Sleep there too. It is the same condition the branch below already treats
as the moment to wait, and playback that has audio to output never
reaches it.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerAudio.cpp
@@ -289,7 +289,12 @@ void CVideoPlayerAudio::Process()
 
       // if we only wanted priority messages, this isn't a stall
       if (priority)
+      {
+        if (timeout == 0ms)
+          CThread::Sleep(10ms);
+
         continue;
+      }
 
       if (m_processInfo.IsTempoAllowed(static_cast<float>(m_speed)/DVD_PLAYSPEED_NORMAL) &&
           !m_stalled && m_syncState == IDVDStreamPlayer::SYNC_INSYNC)
